  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/0629601_sol..jpg\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 82px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Net magnetic field will be at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>The direction of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;velocity&nbsp;of charge is same, hence charge will experience no force.</p>",
